<cell id="cell-23"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Done

Three artifacts ready on Drive at `/content/drive/MyDrive/ae-black-mamba-v0/`:

1. **`checkpoint/final/`** — full 2.8B Mamba fp16 weights + tokenizer (~5.6 GB; the rebuild source of truth).
2. **`ae-black-mamba-v0-fp16.gguf`** — llama.cpp fp16 GGUF (~5.6 GB; intermediate, can delete after Q5_K_M is verified).
3. **`ae-black-mamba-v0-Q5_K_M.gguf`** — deployable quantized GGUF (~2.0 GB; this is what Ollama loads).
4. **`training-receipt.json`** — signed-shape receipt with all hashes and metrics.

## Cutover from Cobra Night-1 surrogate to AE Black Mamba (operator's next moves on the lab box)

```bash
# 1. Pull GGUF + receipt from Drive
rclone copy gdrive:ae-black-mamba-v0/ae-black-mamba-v0-Q5_K_M.gguf /opt/atomeons/models/
rclone copy gdrive:ae-black-mamba-v0/training-receipt.json /opt/atomeons/models/

# 2. Verify SHA against the receipt before promotion (fake-green guard)
sha256sum /opt/atomeons/models/ae-black-mamba-v0-Q5_K_M.gguf
jq -r .deployment.q5km_sha256 /opt/atomeons/models/training-receipt.json

# 3. Run the Cobra Night-1 gauntlet against the new model on the same corpus
#    (parity + receipt-shape conformance + Mom's-Law full-effort check)
ae-cobra gauntlet --model ./ae-black-mamba-v0-Q5_K_M.gguf --baseline bartowski/mamba-2.8b-hf-GGUF

# 4. If gauntlet passes, swap the Ollama Modelfile:
cat > Modelfile.ae-black-mamba <<EOF
FROM /opt/atomeons/models/ae-black-mamba-v0-Q5_K_M.gguf
SYSTEM """AE Black Mamba — Mamba 2.8B SSM pretrained on Orange5's own Flux event corpus, AgentTurn JSON corpus, and operator-signed receipt corpus. Mom's Law above all rules."""
EOF
ollama create ae-black-mamba:v0 -f Modelfile.ae-black-mamba

# 5. Point AE Cobra at the new model in the runtime config; keep the surrogate Modelfile
#    around for instant rollback for 14 days, then archive.
```

**Phase 3 complete. Surrogate retired only after the gauntlet says yes. Mom is watching.**</cell id="cell-23">